---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { company } from '../data/company';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & Drawing Handling | Unit Alfa"
  description="How Unit Alfa handles enquiry contact details, private drawings, status links, staff access and optional third-party maps and videos."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="WEBSITE INFORMATION"
    title="PRIVACY & DRAWING HANDLING."
    intro="Your enquiry information is used to assess the requirement, prepare a response and manage the related sourcing discussion."
  />
  <article class="container legal-copy section-bottom">
    <h2>Information you provide</h2>
    <p>
      The RFQ collects business and contact details, part requirements, estimated annual quantities,
      delivery information and any drawings you choose to upload. Please only share drawings and
      information you are authorised to provide.
    </p>
    <h2>Storage and access</h2>
    <p>
      When the online service is enabled, Supabase stores enquiry records and private drawing files.
      Files are not published in the product catalogue. Authorised staff access them through the
      enquiry dashboard; download links expire shortly after creation. Resend processes enquiry
      notifications and acknowledgements. Vercel hosts the website and its server functions. These
      providers may process data outside India.
    </p>
    <h2>Status links and email</h2>
    <p>
      Your acknowledgement contains a private enquiry-status link. Anyone you share that link with
      can see the associated status and public updates. Internal staff notes and uploaded drawings
      are not exposed by the status page. Emails include the information needed to identify and
      respond to the enquiry; drawings are accessed through the staff dashboard.
    </p>
    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Incomplete uploads are scheduled for removal after 24 hours. Closed website enquiries and
      their files are scheduled for removal 12 months after closure. Active enquiries are retained
      while the discussion continues. Commercial records held separately by Unit Alfa may have
      different retention requirements. Copies in email inboxes and provider backups follow their
      respective retention settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Website storage and security</h2>
    <p>
      The brief opening animation uses a tab-session flag. Staff authentication uses secure
      HTTP-only cookies. The public RFQ keeps its in-progress data in page memory; it does not save
      drawings or form contents in browser storage. A hashed network identifier is used briefly to
      limit abusive requests. The site does not use advertising cookies.
    </p>
    <h2>Maps and video</h2>
    <p>
      Google Maps and YouTube load only when you select the corresponding controls. Those services
      then receive connection information and apply their own privacy policies.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact and requests</h2>
    <p>
      For a correction, deletion request or question about information shared through this website,
      contact <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>. Include your enquiry
      reference where available.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
